sol:'$1\\,\\mu\\text{Ci} = 10^{-6}\\,\\text{Ci} = 10^{-6} \\times 3.7 \\times 10^{10} = 3.7 \\times 10^{4}$ disintegrations per second $= 3.7 \\times 10^{4}\\,\\text{Bq}$. The curie was bolted to the activity of one gram of radium; the becquerel is simply one decay per second.',
