sol:'Each half-life multiplies the population by $1/2$: after $3T_{1/2}$ the survivors number $N_0 \\times (1/2)^3 = N_0/8$. The curve in the figure stair-steps through $N_0/2$ at $T$, $N_0/4$ at $2T$ and $N_0/8$ at $3T$ — exponential decay is just halving stacked on halving.',
